[center][size=6][b]Norse Sense[/b][/size]
[size=4][color=#8ab4f8]Common sense for Vikings: see what the game knows but never shows you.[/color][/size]
[/center]

[line]

Ever built a wall, gone to bed and woken up to a Greydwarf [i]inside[/i] your base?

[b]Norse Sense[/b] shows you what Valheim keeps hidden: where mobs can spawn, how much of your base is protected, whether raids can reach you, how much comfort a piece adds and why a portal won't let you through. Spawn-proof your base, build precisely and keep your map tidy.

Most of it only shows information the game already uses. Nothing is unlocked, spawned or made free unless you turn it on yourself.

[b][color=#80ff80]✔ Client-side only[/color][/b]: works on vanilla servers and alongside players without the mod.
[b][color=#80ff80]✔ Vanilla balance[/color][/b]: no cheats; balance-changing options are off by default.
[b][color=#80ff80]✔ Plays nice with other mods[/color][/b]: detects overlapping mods and adjusts itself.

[line]

[size=5][b]🛡 Spawn View[/b][/size]  [color=#aaaaaa](F7)[/color]

The ground around you is coloured using the game's own spawn rules:
[list]
[*][color=#5090ff][b]Blue: protected.[/b][/color] Inside the range of a workbench, fire or other base piece. Nothing spawns here.
[*][color=#ff5030][b]Red: exposed.[/b][/color] Mobs can spawn here.
[*][color=#ffd040][b]Yellow: steep.[/b][/color] Too steep for most mobs.
[*][b]No colour:[/b] covered by a building or rock, so nothing spawns there either.
[/list]

[b]Also includes:[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Map overlay:[/b] the same colours on your minimap and the large map.
[*][b]Placement preview:[/b] while holding a workbench or campfire, the area it [i]will[/i] protect pulses on the ground, so you can find the best spot before you build.
[*][b]Base rings[/b] around every piece that blocks spawns.
[*][b]Nests, bone piles and creature spawners[/b] are marked. Nests ignore workbenches, so you'll need to destroy them.
[*][b]Raid check:[/b] tells you whether raids can target you where you stand (you need 3+ base pieces nearby), and shows the area of an active raid.
[*][b]Legend[/b] with coverage % and how much exposed ground is left.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]🔨 Building[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Fine rotation:[/b] hold [b]Left Alt[/b] and scroll to rotate in 5° steps instead of 22.5°. Snapping still works.
[*][b]Match rotation:[/b] [b]Left Alt + T[/b] copies the exact angle of the piece you're looking at. Perfect for angled builds.
[*][b]Comfort preview:[/b] when placing a chair, banner or rug, see the comfort level you'll have after placing it, or why it won't add any.
[*][b]Removal lock[/b] [color=#aaaaaa](F9)[/color]: stops the hammer from removing pieces, so you can't delete your build by accident.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]🗺 Cartography Table[/b][/size]

Tired of your map drowning in other players' markers?
[list]
[*][b]Import filters:[/b] skip crossed-out markers, merge duplicates, skip whole icon types, or take only the explored map.
[*][b]Live updates:[/b] shared markers you already have are updated when someone renames, re-icons or crosses them out. Vanilla never does this.
[*][b]Marker manager[/b] [color=#aaaaaa](Left Shift + E at a table)[/color]: search, filter and sort every marker on the table. Rename, change icons, cross out or delete in bulk. The [b]duplicate finder[/b] cleans up a cluttered table in one click.
[*][b]Safe by design:[/b] writing to a table never deletes other players' markers, and the manager merges your edits with the table's current data. Only the table's builder, players permitted on a ward covering it, and admins can edit.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]⛵ Ships & 🌀 Portals[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Hull readout[/b] while you're aboard, and [b]hull warnings[/b] when your ship takes damage or gets critical.
[*][b]Portal item check:[/b] look at a portal and see exactly what's stopping you, e.g. [i]Can't teleport: Copper ore x30, Tin x12[/i].
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]⌨ Keys[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]F7:[/b] toggle spawn view
[*][b]F8:[/b] toggle build info
[*][b]F9:[/b] toggle removal lock
[*][b]Left Alt + scroll:[/b] fine rotation
[*][b]Left Alt + T:[/b] match or reset rotation
[*][b]Left Shift + E[/b] at a cartography table: marker manager
[/list]
All keys and features can be changed or turned off in [b]BepInEx/config/NorseSense.cfg[/b], or in game with Configuration Manager (F1).

[line]

[size=5][b]⚙ Optional tweaks[/b][/size] [color=#aaaaaa](off by default)[/color]
[list]
[*]Stamina cost multiplier for building (hammer) and planting (cultivator).
[*]Build distance and auto-pickup range.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]📋 Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Valheim[/b] 1.0.20 or newer (tested on 1.0.20).
[*][b]BepInExPack for Valheim[/b] 5.4.2351 or newer: the mod loader. [b]Required.[/b]
[*][i]Optional:[/i] [b]Configuration Manager[/b], to change settings in game with F1.
[/list]
[b]Not required on the server.[/b] Only the players who want the features need it, and players without it can play alongside you.

[line]

[size=5][b]📦 Installation[/b][/size]

[b]With Vortex (recommended)[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install [b]BepInExPack for Valheim[/b] with Vortex if you don't have it yet.
[*]Click [b]Mod manager download[/b] on the Files tab, then enable Norse Sense in Vortex.
[*]Start the game and press [b]F7[/b] in your base.
[/list]

[b]Manual[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install [b]BepInExPack for Valheim[/b]: extract it into your Valheim folder and start the game once so it creates its folders. To find your Valheim folder, right-click Valheim in Steam → [i]Manage[/i] → [i]Browse local files[/i].
[*]Download Norse Sense and extract the zip [b]into your Valheim folder[/b]. You should end up with [b]Valheim/BepInEx/plugins/NorseSense/NorseSense.dll[/b].
[*]Start the game and press [b]F7[/b] in your base to check it's working.
[/list]

[b]Updating:[/b] install the new version over the old one. Your settings are kept.
[b]Uninstalling:[/b] delete [b]BepInEx/plugins/NorseSense[/b] (and optionally [b]BepInEx/config/NorseSense.cfg[/b]). Nothing is saved into your world or character, so it's safe to remove at any time.

[b]Troubleshooting:[/b] if F7 does nothing, open [b]BepInEx/LogOutput.log[/b] and look for [i]Loading [Norse Sense[/i]. If it isn't there, BepInEx isn't installed correctly or the DLL is in the wrong folder.

[line]

[size=5][b]🤝 Compatibility[/b][/size]
Norse Sense only adds to the game's code and never replaces it, so other mods' changes to the same code still run. When you load into a world, it checks for overlaps:
[list]
[*][b]Gizmo:[/b] fine rotation turns itself off.
[*][b]Valheim Plus:[/b] build distance and pickup range are left to Valheim Plus.
[*][b]CartographyAdmin:[/b] the marker manager turns itself off.
[*][b]Spawn That, Custom Raids, Expand World[/b] or any mod changing spawn/raid rules: the legend warns that the overlay may not be exact.
[/list]
Tested alongside [b]MyLittleUI[/b], [b]Quick Stack Store[/b] and [b]CameraMod[/b].

[line]

[center][size=3]Found a bug or have an idea? Post in the [b]Bugs[/b] or [b]Posts[/b] tab, and include your [b]BepInEx/LogOutput.log[/b] if something breaks.
[color=#aaaaaa]Endorsements are hugely appreciated. ❤[/color][/size][/center]
